# IPD Patient Flow

IPD owns the inpatient admission record, ward movement, service routing, and discharge readiness; keep every inpatient action attached to one admission and treat overlays as extensions of that record.

## Stage Sequence

- `ADMITTED_PENDING_BED`: admission exists, bed not assigned.
- `ADMITTED_IN_BED`: patient admitted to a ward bed.
- `TRANSFER_REQUESTED` / `TRANSFER_IN_PROGRESS`: internal move pending or underway.
- `DISCHARGE_PLANNED`: discharge work started.
- `DISCHARGED`: encounter complete.
- ICU and theater overlays may appear but must not create parallel records.

## Handoffs

- Admission desk owns registration, source verification, and bed requests.
- Bed manager owns allocation, transfer completion, and bed release.
- Ward nurse owns admission receive, observations, and clearance support.
- Doctor owns assessment, orders, transfers, and discharge planning.
- Billing and pharmacy own clearance checks only and must not advance clinical stages.

## Hard Invariants

- Must keep the IPD encounter as the central inpatient record.
- Must not duplicate OPD, emergency, ICU, or theater encounters.
- Must not mark discharge complete until clearance finishes.
- Must not hide pending results, alerts, or transfer state from the admission view.

## Allowed Critical Actions

- Start ICU stay only when the admission is eligible and an ICU bed is assigned.
- Use `clinical_actions` so lab, radiology, and pharmacy share one source of truth.
- Show discharge readiness early, but keep clearance steps separate.

